{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"Prostate cancer is a disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in the tissues of the prostate.","source_span":"Prostate cancer is a disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in the tissues of the prostate."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"In the U.S., about 1 out of 5 men will be diagnosed with prostate cancer.","source_span":"In the U.S., about 1 out of 5 men will be diagnosed with prostate cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"The prostate is about the size of a walnut and surrounds part of the urethra.","source_span":"It is about the size of a walnut and surrounds part of the urethra"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"The prostate gland makes fluid that is part of the semen.","source_span":"The prostate gland makes fluid that is part of the semen."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"Signs of prostate cancer include a weak flow of urine or frequent urination.","source_span":"Signs of prostate cancer include a weak flow of urine or frequent urination."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH) occurs when the aging prostate enlarges and blocks the urethra or bladder; it is not cancer but surgery may be needed.","source_span":"The condition is called benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), and although it is not cancer, surgery may be needed."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"The Gleason score ranges from 2-10 and describes how likely a tumor is to spread; the lower the number, the less likely the tumor is to spread.","source_span":"The Gleason score ranges from 2-10 and describes how likely it is that a tumor will spread. The lower the number, the less likely the tumor is to spread."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"A transrectal biopsy is the removal of tissue from the prostate by inserting a thin needle through the rectum and into the prostate.","source_span":"A transrectal biopsy is the removal of tissue from the prostate by inserting a thin needle through the rectum and into the prostate."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"PSA levels may also be high in men who have an infection or inflammation of the prostate or BPH, not just prostate cancer.","source_span":"PSA levels may also be high in men who have an infection or inflammation of the prostate or BPH (an enlarged, but noncancerous, prostate)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"Transrectal ultrasound uses a probe to bounce high-energy sound waves off internal tissues to form a picture called a sonogram.","source_span":"The probe is used to bounce high-energy sound waves (ultrasound) off internal tissues or organs and make echoes. The echoes form a picture of body tissues called a sonogram."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"Cancer stage, including PSA level, Gleason score, tumor grade, extent of prostate involvement, and spread, affects prognosis.","source_span":"The stage of the cancer (level of PSA, Gleason score, grade of the tumor, how much of the prostate is affected by the cancer, and whether the cancer has spread to other places in the body)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"Most men diagnosed with prostate cancer do not die of it.","source_span":"Most men diagnosed with prostate cancer do not die of it."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","statement":"Prostate cancer is staged using four stages: Stage I, Stage II, Stage III, and Stage IV.","source_span":"Stage I     - Stage II     - Stage III     - Stage IV"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What is prostate cancer?","answer":"Prostate cancer is a disease in which malignant (cancer) cells form in the tissues of the prostate."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","fact_refs":[1],"question":"In the United States, roughly how many men will be diagnosed with prostate cancer?","answer":"About 1 out of 5 men in the U.S. will be diagnosed with prostate cancer."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What range does the Gleason score cover, and what does a lower score mean?","answer":"The Gleason score ranges from 2 to 10, and the lower the number, the less likely the tumor is to spread."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What is a transrectal biopsy?","answer":"A transrectal biopsy is the removal of tissue from the prostate by inserting a thin needle through the rectum and into the prostate."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","fact_refs":[10],"question":"What stage-related factors affect a prostate cancer patient's prognosis?","answer":"Prognosis depends on the stage of the cancer, including PSA level, Gleason score, tumor grade, how much of the prostate is affected, and whether the cancer has spread to other parts of the body."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_1","fact_refs":[12],"question":"What are the four stages used to classify prostate cancer?","answer":"Prostate cancer is staged as Stage I, Stage II, Stage III, or Stage IV."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"Prostate cancer is the second most common cancer among men in the United States.","source_span":"Prostate cancer is the second most common cancer among men in the United States."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"In the U.S., about one out of five men will be diagnosed with prostate cancer.","source_span":"In the U.S., about one out of five men will be diagnosed with prostate cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"Prostate cancer is rare in men younger than 50 years of age.","source_span":"Prostate cancer is rare in men younger than 50 years of age."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"A man whose father, brother, or son has had prostate cancer has a higher-than-average risk of prostate cancer.","source_span":"A man whose father, brother, or son has had prostate cancer has a higher-than-average risk of prostate cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"Prostate cancer occurs more often in African-American men than in white men.","source_span":"Prostate cancer occurs more often in African-American men than in white men."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"African-American men with prostate cancer are more likely to die from the disease than white men with prostate cancer.","source_span":"African-American men with prostate cancer are more likely to die from the disease than white men with prostate cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"DHT (dihydrotestosterone) is important for normal prostate growth but can also cause the prostate to enlarge and may contribute to prostate cancer development.","source_span":"DHT is important for normal prostate growth but can also cause the prostate to get bigger and may play a part in the development of prostate cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"The SELECT trial found that vitamin E taken alone increased the risk of prostate cancer, and the risk continued even after men stopped taking it.","source_span":"The Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial (SELECT) found that vitamin E taken alone increased the risk of prostate cancer. The risk continued even after the men stopped taking vitamin E."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"A 10-year study showed the risk of prostate cancer was increased in men who took 1 milligram (mg) supplements of folic acid.","source_span":"A 10-year study showed that the risk of prostate cancer was increased in men who took 1 milligram (mg) supplements of folic acid."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"The risk of prostate cancer was lower in men who had enough folate in their diets.","source_span":"However, the risk of prostate cancer was lower in men who had enough folate in their diets."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"Finasteride and dutasteride are drugs that lower the amount of male sex hormones made by the body by blocking the enzyme that changes testosterone into DHT.","source_span":"Finasteride and dutasteride are drugs used to lower the amount of male sex hormones made by the body. These drugs block the enzyme that changes testosterone into dihydrotestosterone (DHT)."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"Taking finasteride or dutasteride has been shown to lower the risk for prostate cancer, but it is not known if these drugs lower the risk of death from prostate cancer.","source_span":"Taking finasteride or dutasteride has been shown to lower the risk for prostate cancer, but it is not known if these drugs lower the risk of death from prostate cancer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"The Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial (PCPT) studied whether finasteride can prevent prostate cancer in healthy men 55 years of age and older.","source_span":"The Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial (PCPT) studied whether the drug finasteride can prevent prostate cancer in healthy men 55 years of age and older."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"In the PCPT, men who took finasteride had fewer prostate cancers, but those who did develop cancer had more aggressive tumors, and the number of deaths from prostate cancer was the same in both groups.","source_span":"This prevention study showed there were fewer prostate cancers in the group of men that took finasteride compared with the group of men that did not. Also, the men who took finasteride who did have prostate cancer had more aggressive tumors. The number of deaths from prostate cancer was the same in both groups."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"Men who took finasteride in the PCPT reported more side effects, including erectile dysfunction, loss of desire for sex, and enlarged breasts.","source_span":"Men who took finasteride reported more side effects compared with the group of men that did not, including erectile dysfunction, loss of desire for sex, and enlarged breasts."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"The REDUCE trial studied whether dutasteride can prevent prostate cancer in men aged 50 to 75 years at higher risk for the disease.","source_span":"The Reduction by Dutasteride of Prostate Cancer Events Trial (REDUCE) studied whether the drug dutasteride can prevent prostate cancer in men aged 50 to 75 years at higher risk for the disease."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","statement":"The REDUCE trial found fewer prostate cancers in the group of men who took dutasteride compared with the group that did not.","source_span":"This prevention study showed there were fewer prostate cancers in the group of men who took dutasteride compared with the group of men that did not."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What rank does prostate cancer hold among cancers affecting men in the United States?","answer":"Prostate cancer is the second most common cancer among men in the United States."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What did the SELECT trial find about taking vitamin E alone and prostate cancer risk?","answer":"The SELECT trial found that vitamin E taken alone increased the risk of prostate cancer, and the increased risk continued even after men stopped taking vitamin E."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","fact_refs":[8,9],"question":"What did a 10-year study find about folic acid supplements versus getting enough folate from diet, in relation to prostate cancer risk?","answer":"The study found that taking 1 mg folic acid supplements increased prostate cancer risk, while men who had enough folate in their diets had a lower risk."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","fact_refs":[12,13],"question":"Who did the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial (PCPT) study, and what did it find about finasteride?","answer":"The PCPT studied healthy men aged 55 and older; it found fewer prostate cancers among men who took finasteride, but those who did develop cancer had more aggressive tumors, and the number of deaths from prostate cancer was the same in both groups."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","fact_refs":[14],"question":"What side effects did men taking finasteride report more often in the PCPT?","answer":"Men who took finasteride reported more erectile dysfunction, loss of desire for sex, and enlarged breasts compared with men who did not take it."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","fact_refs":[15,16],"question":"What did the REDUCE trial study, and what did it find about dutasteride?","answer":"The REDUCE trial studied whether dutasteride could prevent prostate cancer in men aged 50 to 75 at higher risk, and found fewer prostate cancers in the men who took dutasteride than in those who did not."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000036_2","fact_refs":[4,5],"question":"How does prostate cancer risk and mortality differ between African-American men and white men?","answer":"Prostate cancer occurs more often in African-American men than in white men, and African-American men with prostate cancer are more likely to die from it than white men with prostate cancer."}
